  abstract     = {Crizotinib (1), an anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK) receptor
                  tyrosine kinase inhibitor approved by the U.S. Food and Drug
                  Administration in 2011, is efficacious in ALK and ROS positive
                  patients. Under pressure of crizotinib treatment, point
                  mutations arise in the kinase domain of ALK, resulting in
                  resistance and progressive disease. The successful application
