                  physician. The most frequently used definition of "current
                  asthma" was "asthma ever" and either asthma symptoms or asthma
                  medications in the last 12 months. This definition of "current
                  asthma" was used in 16 cohorts. There was no statistically
                  significant difference in the pooled asthma prevalence in
