                  participants (10-85th percentile, T2D, glycated haemoglobin
                  [HbA1c ] 7.0\%-11.0\% [if diet- and exercise-treated] or 6.5\%
                  to 11.0\% [if treated with metformin, basal insulin or both])
                  to liraglutide or placebo. This post-hoc analysis evaluated
                  changes from baseline to weeks 26 and 52 in absolute BMI,
                  percent change in BMI and other weight-related parameters.
                  Changes were assessed by liraglutide overall (all doses) and
                  liraglutide by dose (0.6, 1.2 and 1.8 mg/day) vs placebo using
                  a pattern mixture model of observed data, with missing
                  observations imputed from each treatment group. RESULTS: In
                  total, 134 participants were included. There were
                  statistically significant differences between groups in
