  abstract     = {Abstract During the last decade, there have been substantial
                  advances in the identification and characterization of DNA
                  sequence variants associated with individual predisposition to
                  type 1 and type 2 diabetes. As well as providing insights into
                  the molecular, cellular, and physiological mechanisms involved
                  in disease pathogenesis, these risk variants, when combined
