  journaltitle = {Int. J. Epidemiol.},
  volume       = {43},
  issue        = {4},
  pages        = {1082--1088},
  date         = {2014-08},
  abstract     = {In this paper we update the profile of the 1993 Pelotas
                  (Brazil) Birth Cohort Study, with emphasis on a shift of
                  priority from maternal and child health research topics to
                  four main categories of outcome variables, collected
                  throughout adolescence: (i) mental health; (ii) body
                  composition; (iii) risk factors for non-communicable diseases
                  (NCDs); (iv) human capital. We were able to trace 81.3\% (n =
                  4106) of the original cohort at 18 years of age. For the first
                  time, the 18-years visit took place entirely on the university
                  premises, in a clinic equipped with state-of-the-art equipment
