                  children's anthropometric measurements were
                  evaluated.ResultsOf 1650 children identified, 1212 were
                  evaluated (response rate, 73.4\%), and 21 died before the
                  baseline assessment. The age of the offspring ranged from 0 to
                  10 years (mean [±SD], 2.9 ± 2.1 years); most children (65.6\%)
