  pages        = {572--580},
  date         = {2012-08-11},
  abstract     = {BACKGROUND: High plasma HDL cholesterol is associated with
                  reduced risk of myocardial infarction, but whether this
                  association is causal is unclear. Exploiting the fact that
                  genotypes are randomly assigned at meiosis, are independent of
                  non-genetic confounding, and are unmodified by disease
                  processes, mendelian randomisation can be used to test the
