  date         = {2015-04-30},
  abstract     = {The convergence of two rapidly developing technologies -
                  high-throughput genotyping and electronic health records
                  (EHRs) - gives scientists an unprecedented opportunity to
                  utilize routine healthcare data to accelerate genomic
                  discovery. Institutions and healthcare systems have been
                  building EHR-linked DNA biobanks to enable such a vision.
