  issue        = {1},
  pages        = {29--35},
  date         = {2018-02},
  abstract     = {Motivation: Epidemiological cohorts typically contain a
                  diverse set of phenotypes such that automation of phenome
                  scans is non-trivial, because they require highly
                  heterogeneous models. For this reason, phenome scans have to
                  date tended to use a smaller homogeneous set of phenotypes
                  that can be analysed in a consistent fashion. We present
                  PHESANT (PHEnome Scan ANalysis Tool), a software package for
                  performing comprehensive phenome scans in UK Biobank. General
                  features: PHESANT tests the association of a specified trait
                  with all continuous, integer and categorical variables in UK
                  Biobank, or a specified subset. PHESANT uses a novel
