  issue        = {5},
  pages        = {550--560},
  date         = {2000-09},
  abstract     = {In observational studies with exposures or treatments that
                  vary over time, standard approaches for adjustment of
                  confounding are biased when there exist time-dependent
                  confounders that are also affected by previous treatment. This
