  volume       = {365},
  issue        = {9464},
  pages        = {1099--1104},
  date         = {2005},
  abstract     = {The gross inequalities in health that we see within and
                  between countries present a challenge to the world. That there
                  should be a spread of life expectancy of 48 years among
                  countries and 20 years or more within countries is not
                  inevitable. A burgeoning volume of research identifies social
                  factors at the root of much of these inequalities in health.
